            "id": "4957196",
            "title": "Fed Decision, Microsoft, Alphabet Earnings Highlight Blockbuster Week",
            "description": "<html><body><p data-eci=\"true\">Get ahead of the market by subscribing to Seeking Alpha's Wall Street Week Ahead, a preview of key events scheduled for the coming week. The newsletter keeps you informed of the biggest stories set to make headlines, including upcoming IPOs, investor days, earnings reports, and conference presentations.</p> <p class=\"MsoNormal\">Wall Street heads into a blockbuster week with a Federal Reserve interest rate decision, the first read on Q3 GDP, and earnings from some of the world's largest tech companies all on deck.</p> <p class=\"MsoNormal\">Stocks ended a volatile week lower on Friday as investors continued to question the cost and potential returns from the AI investment boom. The S&amp;P 500 (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/SP500\" title=\"S&amp;P 500 Index\">SP500</a>) fell 0.5% for the week, and the Nasdaq (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/COMP:IND\" title=\"NASDAQ Composite Index\">COMP:IND</a>) declined 0.7%, while technology shares were hit particularly hard on Thursday amid renewed concerns over AI spending.</p> <p class=\"MsoNormal\">The Federal Reserve takes center stage Wednesday, with policymakers scheduled to announce their irate decision at 2 p.m. ET, followed by Chairman Kevin Warsh's press conference at 2:30 p.m. Fed funds futures imply only a 10% probability of another 25-basis-point increase after the central bank raised rates in September.</p> <p class=\"MsoNormal\">The economic calendar gets busier Thursday, when investors receive the first estimate of Q3 GDP and the October core PCE price index. Economists expect annualized GDP growth of 3.0%, while the headline PCE inflation rate is forecast at 3.1%.</p> <p class=\"MsoNormal\">Earnings will provide an equally important test for markets. Alphabet (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/GOOG\" title=\"Alphabet Inc.\">GOOG</a>) (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/GOOGL\" title=\"Alphabet Inc.\">GOOGL</a>) and Microsoft (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/MSFT\" title=\"Microsoft Corporation\">MSFT</a>) report Wednesday, followed by Amazon (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/AMZN\" title=\"Amazon.com, Inc.\">AMZN</a>) Thursday, putting AI spending, cloud demand, and the return on massive datacenter investments firmly back in focus.</p> <p class=\"MsoNormal\">______________________________________________________________</p> <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>Earnings spotlight:</strong> Monday, Oct. 26: Verizon (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/VZ\" title=\"Verizon Communications Inc.\">VZ</a>), Welltower (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/WELL\" title=\"Welltower Inc.\">WELL</a>), Nucor (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/NUE\" title=\"Nucor Corporation\">NUE</a>), Public Storage (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/PSA\" title=\"Public Storage\">PSA</a>). <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/earnings/earnings-calendar\">See the full earnings calendar</a>.</p> <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>Earnings spotlight:</strong> Tuesday, Oct. 27: Visa (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/V\" title=\"Visa Inc.\">V</a>), Coca-Cola (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/KO\" title=\"The Coca-Cola Company\">KO</a>), Boeing (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/BA\" title=\"The Boeing Company\">BA</a>), UPS (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/UPS\" title=\"United Parcel Service, Inc.\">UPS</a></p></body></html>",
